Syllables with apostrophes do count. Syllables whose nucleus is just "y" do=
=20
not count, unless they're the last syllable (which never occurs in brivla).=
=20
Consonantal syllables don't count at all. The correct stress is "rodbO'e".

A diphthong counts as only one syllable, even if pronounced as two, thus th=
e=20
stress of "spatrxapio" is "spatrxApio" even if you pronounce=20
it "spat,r,xa,pi,o". (The same applies in Spanish, by the way. "apio" is=20
stressed on "a". And some past tenses of verbs ending in "-i=F3" are pronou=
nced=20
with "-i,=F3".)

